
This file is divided into three parts:  the first section explains 
features of Strategic Falcon that were included too late to make it 
into the manual, the second corrects some errata in the manual, and 
the third part offers troubleshooting advice.


                     -----------------------
                     "Undocumented Features"
                     -----------------------

Mission Description:

If you would like to refresh your memory about the description for 
the current mission, press <F2> at any time (<F1> is "reserved for 
future use").

If you want to change the mission description, you can do so with 
any text editor.  Just edit the SQUAD?.MTV file of the appropriate 
squad (use the technique described below in the second trouble-
shooting question to find out which squad number belongs in place of 
the "?").  Keep any descriptions short!


Timing Trace:

In order to allow you to get a better feel for how a mission should
pan out, the Map screen in the "Other" mode includes a button 
called "Timing."  If you press this button, symbols move along the 
flight paths.  The symbols' speed is tied to the speed setting of 
the applicable waypoint.  Therefore, in a "pure" mission, your 
aircraft (and the enemy aircraft) will be in the positions 
indicated relative to each other.  This allows you to time your 
flights with a great deal of precision.

To speed up the trace speed, press the "+" button;  to slow it 
down, press the "-" button.

To freeze the display at any point, press the "Pause" button and 
hold it down;  when you release it, the trace will resume.  To 
abort the trace before it finishes, press the "Timing" button 
again. 

Of course, this screen doesn't take into account any random 
aircraft, nor does it compensate for the reaction of the enemy to 
your presence!  Also, "Loiter" waypoints are not supported--which 
means when a flight reaches the end of its path, it'll stop, 
regardless of the action assigned to the final waypoint. 

If you're interested, each time a symbol "jumps," it repesents 
four seconds of flight time.


Fuller Backups:

In addition to backing up the MIS, CAM, and WAR files for the 
current campaign, StratFalc also backs up the SQU and MTV files.
This allows the RESTRCAM batch file (explained below) to fully 
restore your campaign, even if you've moved on to another mission.  
For instance, "SQUAD0.MTV" becomes "SQU0MTV.BAK," and "SQUAD0.SQU" 
becomes "SQU0SQU.BAK." 



